WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:14.503
carried his talking wood home carefully.

2
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:17.064
Geppetto's home was simple and clean.

3
00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:21.687
He had one large room with a bed, a table, his tools, and a stove.

4
00:00:22.407 --> 00:00:25.429
Although Geppetto worked hard, he did not have very much money.

5
00:00:26.129 --> 00:00:27.030
But he didn't mind.

6
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.832
"Now, where should I start?"

7
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:32.329
he wondered aloud.

8
00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:35.210
"I've never made a boy before."

9
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.991
"Start with the legs!

10
00:00:37.431 --> 00:00:39.332
That way I can run fast!"

11
00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:40.353
said the wood.

12
00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:46.737
"No, I think you had better have eyes first, so you don't run into walls.

13
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:50.659
I don't want you to get hurt," Geppetto said.

14
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.841
He was happy to be making his very own boy.

15
00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:59.644
He started first by carving out the face, and then he carved the eyes.

16
00:01:00.516 --> 00:01:05.378
As the wood looked more like a boy's face, he became excited about what he and his boy

17
00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.078
could do together.

18
00:01:06.778 --> 00:01:07.838
What fun they would have!

19
00:01:07.858 --> 00:01:13.300
"There, your eyes look very smart.

20
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.260
How well can you see?"

21
00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:16.601
Geppetto asked.

22
00:01:16.621 --> 00:01:19.602
"Oh, it's terrible!"

23
00:01:20.002 --> 00:01:20.622
cried the wood.

24
00:01:20.642 --> 00:01:22.463
"What's wrong?"

25
00:01:23.023 --> 00:01:24.043
asked Geppetto, worried.

26
00:01:25.163 --> 00:01:26.664
He thought maybe the wood was blind.

27
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.280
"We are very poor!

28
00:01:30.861 --> 00:01:32.341
Look at this small room!

29
00:01:33.161 --> 00:01:36.422
I want to be rich, not poor," the wood said.

30
00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:39.623
Geppetto was sad that his boy was ashamed of his home.

31
00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:42.824
He promised himself that his boy would have whatever he needed.

32
00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:49.786
"I will carve out your ears next, so that you can hear and learn," Geppetto said.

33
00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:53.147
Geppetto worked carefully on the wood all through the day.

34
00:01:53.827 --> 00:01:57.288
He carved hair, a nose, and a smile before lunch.

35
00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.462
Then, he shared his first meal of bread and cheese with his boy.

36
00:02:01.482 --> 00:02:08.767
"You and I will have great fun together, boy," said Geppetto as he ate his meal.

37
00:02:09.387 --> 00:02:11.849
He tore off some bread and put it into the boy's mouth.

38
00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.431
"Only I shouldn't call you 'boy'.

39
00:02:16.232 --> 00:02:17.213
You need a name.

40
00:02:17.893 --> 00:02:19.234
What should we name you?"

41
00:02:19.254 --> 00:02:21.956
"I know!

42
00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:27.880
My name can be Prince Edmund of the Great Woods," said the wood.

43
00:02:28.608 --> 00:02:30.990
He liked the name because it sounded big and important.

44
00:02:32.571 --> 00:02:35.593
"That is too big a name for such a small boy.

45
00:02:36.494 --> 00:02:40.317
Since you are made of pinewood, I will call you Pinocchio.

46
00:02:41.097 --> 00:02:41.878
What do you think?"

47
00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:43.099
asked Geppetto.

48
00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:45.400
He wanted to pick a name the boy would like.

49
00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:55.548
"Yes—Pinocchio. That sounds important, though it doesn't sound as grand as Prince Edmund of the Great Woods.

50
00:02:56.972 --> 00:02:59.833
I think it will be fine," he agreed.

51
00:02:59.853 --> 00:03:03.254
"Wonderful! Pinocchio it is!

52
00:03:04.394 --> 00:03:08.995
To celebrate, I will carve your arms and legs so we can dance!"

53
00:03:09.876 --> 00:03:11.096
And Geppetto carved quickly.

54
00:03:13.577 --> 00:03:18.858
As soon as Geppetto finished carving Pinocchio's feet, Pinocchio jumped to the floor and ran out of the

55
00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:19.438
front door.

56
00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:22.739
"Wait!" Geppetto called out.

57
00:03:22.759 --> 00:03:25.760
"Pinocchio, where are you going?"

58
00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.181
"I am off to find adventures!"

59
00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:30.401
Pinocchio called.

60
00:03:30.421 --> 00:03:34.262
"But, you don't have any clothes on yet!

61
00:03:34.822 --> 00:03:36.943
You can't run away if you are naked!

62
00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:38.963
Please, don't leave!"

63
00:03:39.584 --> 00:03:41.764
Geppetto cried, as he ran after Pinocchio.

64
00:03:42.364 --> 00:03:45.485
Unfortunately, Geppetto forgot to leave his knife on the table.

65
00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.966
He was running after Pinocchio with his knife still in his hand!

66
00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:56.360
The neighbors thought he wanted to hurt Pinocchio, so they called for the police: "Police, police!

67
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.141
Catch him!"

68
00:03:58.781 --> 00:04:03.564
One of the policemen was nearby, and he ran into the street just in time to catch Geppetto.

69
00:04:04.884 --> 00:04:07.146
He would not let Geppetto explain about Pinocchio.

70
00:04:07.886 --> 00:04:12.028
The policeman was scared of Geppetto's knife, so he threw him in jail for the night.
